cff-version: "1.2.0"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "kitab — a config-driven book-publishing template"
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: "A reusable, config-driven static book template extracted from the tabdili reader architecture. Presentation, content, and data are decoupled; a new book is config plus content. Multi-format readers (paginated, continuous scroll, liquid), self-describing 'talking artifact' figures with pop-out explanations, TTS and BYOK AI-explain, learning-to-doing links, and pure-GitHub-Pages visitor participation."
authors:
